{"resourceIdentifier":"3336","resourceName":"Eastern Yan’an Afforestation Project","description":"Eastern Yan’an Afforestation Project (hereafter referred to as ‘The Project’the project”) is located in Yanchang County, Yanchuan County, Yichuan County and Zichang City  in eastern Yan’an City, Shaanxi Province, People’s Republic of China. The project aims to increase carbon sequestration and improve the local ecological environment by means of forest planting activities on degraded lands suffering from severe soil erosion.\r\nThe project activities involve the planting of trees and shrubs on 58,423.59 hectares (or 876,354 Mu ) of degraded lands located in Yanchang County, Yanchuan County, Yichuan County and Zichang City under the administration of Yan’an City. The species include Robinia pseudoacacia (black locust), Platycladus orientalis (Oriental thuja or Oriental arborvitae), Pinus tabuliformis (Chinese red pine), Armeniaca sibirica (Siberian apricot) as well as Hippophae rhamnoides (sea-buckthorn). All of them are native species except for Robinia pseudoacacia, which is native to North America; it is not considered as an invasive species in China (refer to Section 5.2 for details). The project area was degraded lands with little vegetation before the project and would continue to be so without the implementation of the project activities. \r\nThe implementation of the project activity will generate GHG emission removals and mitigate climate change, improve soil and water conditions, increase the forest cover and enhance local biodiversity; the project also generates social benefits including job opportunities and technical skills training for local communities and residents.","location":{"latitude":36.671554,"longitude":110.128093},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-10-14","endExclusive":"2022-11-14","endInclusive":"2022-11-13"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3336"}]},{"code":"STA